WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.935
Our next guest
is a very talented actress

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.903
who stars as Princess Diana
in the brand-new season

00:00:04.903 --> 00:00:07.973
of "The Crown," which is
streaming right now on Netflix,

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:09.542
and everyone is watching.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.211
Here is Emma Corrin.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.080
Emma, thank you so much
for doing this.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.249
I'm so excited
that you're here.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:19.052
-Hi. Thanks for having me.
I'm excited.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.487
-I was going to ask you
how the last few months

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.889
have been in quarantine,

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.658
but then I saw this photo,

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.660
and I think it pretty much
sums it all up.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.697
You playing cards with your dog.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.466
What stage of quarantine
was this?

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.768
-This was actually
very early quarantine.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.403
-Okay.
-This was, like, peak lockdown.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:40.373
Hadn't been outside the house
in a very long time.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.608
And we found ourselves here,
yeah,

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.011
playing spit
with my little puppy.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.680
-There's a rumor I wanted
to ask you about because --

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.315
And tell me if this is not true.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.217
Again, I get all my info
from Wikipedia.

00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:55.388
And I run the website, so
actually I make up the rumors.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.923
So you should thank me later.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.426
But I was --
Apparently I heard this,

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.728
that you have
a very famous dog walker.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.464
I read -- I don't know if you
know what I'm talking about.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:08.368
I read that Harry Styles
walks your dog.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:09.635
-Ohh.
-Is that true?

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.138
-Yeah. He -- Sort of.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.807
He once dog-sat for me.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:17.743
-[ Laughs ] He did?

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.380
-The thing I love about this
is also my dog has no idea,

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.049
which is I think
the wonderful thing about it.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.483
For a dog, it's just a person.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.753
But, um...

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.621
sort of near where he lives.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.624
And he looked after Spencer
for me.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.659
But not again.
He hasn't done it again.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.961
And I think it's because
halfway through the meal

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:38.665
I got a message that just said,

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.733
"He won't stop farting.
Is this normal?"

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.268
And --

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.504
-Was it from Spencer
or from Harry?

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.874
-[ Laughs ] From Spencer.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.876
"Emma, I'm not
doing this again."

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.845
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.414
How good of a dude
is Harry Styles.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.950
What a nice guy.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.018
Pal, "The Crown"
premiered this weekend.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.487
Everybody I know --
I had to text everyone and go,

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.988
"Stop. Don't tell me. Don't --"

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.057
They're like,
"Yeah, but this happened."

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.826
I go, "Don't tell me anything."

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.494
For anyone who hasn't
watched it yet,

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:11.030
could you set up what's going on
this season of "The Crown"?

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.599
-Yeah, I play Diana from when
she's about 16 years old

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:17.770
to when she's about 28,
so a long, long time.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.973
And, yeah, I love this season
because it follows essentially

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:25.010
three incredibly
brilliant women --

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.080
Well, sort of debatable.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.115
But, well,
very interesting women.

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:31.851
The Queen, Diana, and Thatcher.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.387
And sort of looks
at their relationship

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.956
to power and these powerful
positions they've been put in

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.658
and how they grapple with it.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.762
So, yeah, we see these
sort of stories unfold

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.365
throughout the years
and how they handle it, yeah.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.567
-Well, not only did you get
the look down, the hair,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.471
but the voice was perfection.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.907
And then I read somewhere that
you also do a good Charles.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.576
-I think so.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:00.146
I spent a lot of long time
on set trying to copy Josh.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:03.749
-So, how would you give me
advice on how to do Charles

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:05.651
or how to do Diana?
Could you?

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.753
-Yeah, yeah.
Do you want a lesson?

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.388
Oh, my God. Yeah, sure. Okay.

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:12.258
So, Charles, the thing
they say is to basically --

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.726
If you want to say "yes" --

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.996
If you want to get into his
voice, you say the word "ears."

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.131
Like ears. Ears.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.166
-Oh. Ears.

00:03:21.166 --> 00:03:23.202
-Ears. Ears.
-Ears. Ears.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.137
-And that's how
you're saying "yes," basically.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:28.574
-Wow! That is hilarious
that he says "ears."

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:32.211
-That kind of helps. Ears.
-Ears. Ears.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.747
-And what I always did
for Di was, "All right."

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:38.083
And she always kind of
goes down at the end
of everything she says.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.886
So it'd be like, "All right.
Are you all right?

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.454
I'm all right."

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.691
-[ Laughs ]
See? You're very good.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.225
"I'm all right.
Are you all right?"

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.660
-I'll say to you -- I'll say,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.130
"I'm gonna go in the other room
and watch the news."

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.765
And you say, "All right."
Okay?

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.233
-Okay.
You're going to be Charles?

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.502
-Yeah. For this first scene,
I'll be Charles.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.803
-Okay.

00:03:57.803 --> 00:04:00.072
-Ears. I'll be in the next room
watching the news.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.675
-All right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.243
Great.
-That's pretty good.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.579
Now let's switch it around.
Ready?

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.649
-Okay. So I'm Charles? Okay.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:15.521
Ears. I'm going to go into the
other room and watch the news.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.557
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.560
-You sounded French!

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.695
You sounded like
Inspector Clouseau.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.496
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:26.098
-[French accent]
Do you understand?

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.401
You cannot understand
what I'm doing.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.170
I'm going to the next room
to watch the news!

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.440
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.909
-All right.
-All right!

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.644
-All right!

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.346
-All right!
-Yeah, I can't --

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.581
I don't know who I'm doing.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.449
I'm doing, like,
a bad Cyndi Lauper.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.151
-I don't know what I'm doing.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:49.855
Here is Emma Corrin
in season four of "The Crown."

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.190
Take a look at this.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:55.495
-I suppose the greatest
highlight has been, well,

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:58.798
well, meeting all of you,
the people of Australia.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.866
You've made us feel
so welcome, so at home.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:04.737
-Well, perhaps. Because
you've been so refreshing.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.206
You're not what we expect
from royalty.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.909
-Well, that's because I don't
think of myself as royalty.

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:14.347
First and foremost,
I'm a wife and a mother.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.615
That's what's
most important to me.

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.185
-She really is
a wonderful mother.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.153
-And how's William
getting along?

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:23.322
-Oh, he's having
a magical time here.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.624
-So he likes Australia?
-Let's put it like this.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:28.160
His favorite cuddly toy
used to be a whale,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.030
but since coming here,
it's been firmly supplanted

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.765
by a koala.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.933
-Emma Corrin.
Season four of "The Crown"

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.835
is streaming
right now on Netflix.

00:05:36.835 --> 00:05:39.005
Please come back on
whenever you want to

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.907
and congrats on everything.

